        "detailed_description": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Do what the voice tells you, no matter how wrong it feels.</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You open your eyes to a bare room. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >No windows. No doors. No escape. </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Complete each daily task.</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Only a bed, a table, a bathroom, and a voice that speaks when you wake. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each morning, it gives you a task. At first, they seem harmless—simple chores in a place that shouldn’t exist. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >But by the second day, the tone shifts. The tasks grow darker, more personal, more invasive. You begin to wonder what the voice wants from you—or if it wants you to become something else. </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >How far will you go to survive when there’s no way out?</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The only rule: obey the voice for seven days.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>",
